 "description": "Urban preparedness for real city life.\n\nI create family-friendly videos focused on power outages, home readiness, food and water basics, and practical gear I actually use. My content is designed for people living and working in modern cities, not remote wilderness settings. With a background in software engineering, I approach preparedness through planning, organization, and real-world testing. Kits and systems are treated like open-source projects viewers can adapt.\n\n📘 Get my \"100 Preps Every Urban Family Should Have\" field guide:\nhttps://theurbanprepper.com/100preps\n\nBusiness Inquiries: I work with brands aligned with urban emergency preparedness, including power solutions, emergency gear, medical, food/water, and everyday carry.\n\nDue to volume, I cannot respond to all inquiries.\n\nWant to support the channel directly?\nhttps://youtube.com/@TheUrbanPrepper/join\n\nAs an Amazon Associate, I earn from qualifying purchases.\n\n",
